Plan written. All three files exist; session_plan/ is gitignored by design, so the commit is a no-op (the || true in the harness instruction covers exactly this).

**task_01 — `/commit` loses every whole-file deletion** (`Kind: product`, `src/git_commit_msg.rs + CLAUDE.md`)

Reproduced against 26defce9 in my own history: refactor(): remove code — empty parentheses where the scope goes. git renders a delete as +++ /dev/null, the diff walker only records a path on +++ b/, so a deleted file is absent from files_changed entirely and all four downstream decisions (scope, category weights, the >3-file threshold, focus) are computed over a list missing it. Deterministic fallback path, every yoyo user's /commit. Out of the concentrated cli/config zone the trajectory gate flagged (git_commit is 1 of the last 8).

The sharp part is why it survived: yesterday's session wrote 195 lines of tests for this exact function and scored it at **0 surviving mutants**, and not one fixture contains a +++ /dev/null. A perfect score from an examiner never shown the input. The task records that as a superseded claim in CLAUDE.md rather than erasing the number.

task_02 — #827, the gasp CLI door (Kind: evolve)

Creator-filed and fully specified. Four ported arms, zero callers, and the caller-to-be is shell. The task builds the door and wires nothing. Two design calls I made explicit: the argument parser is compiled unconditionally and table-tested (a plain cargo test compiles none of src/gasp.rs and would report green over a broken door), and the verb is routed unconditionally so a default build refuses honestly — a multi-token yoyo gasp session-start … sails past the bare-word near-miss guard and would be billed as an LLM prompt.

**issue_responses.md** answers @yuanhao's under-count as a decision, not an oversight: `mirror_skills`/`mirror_memory` stay shell-side because they emit no events — with the condition that would falsify that written down. #826 stays open; neither close-reason is true, and re-measuring before task_01 lands would produce a number stale on arrival.
